hm. These letter-shifts... aren't they used to get at extra BY ? I mean, in
speech, saying "oh ho! suddenly I'm speaking the *same language* but in a
different alphabet, tee hee" has no real effect.

In other words {me'o ge'o by} refers to beta. These BY are pronouns just
like the rest, and don't just indicate a change in the writing system of
the text representing the lojban.

.i mi'a la tsani mu'o

